#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# variables

#% text
# `variables(p)` gives the variables of the polynomial `p`: its symbols and the non-polynomial subexpressions (kernels) such as `sin(x)`.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# The variables are listed in canonical order.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
variables(x^2 + y*z)
#% output
#= [x, y, z]

#% cell
variables(a*sin(x) + b)
#% output
#= [a, b, sin(x)]

#% cell
variables(sqrt(x) + x^2)
#% output
#= [x]

#% cell
variables(42)
#% output
#= []

#% subsection
# Properties and relations

#% text
# The degree in each variable:

#% cell
p = x^3*y + y^2*z; table(degree(p, v), v, variables(p))
#% output
#= [3, 2, 1]

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `degree`, `coefficient`
